{% icon id="envelope" size=32 /%}Keep up with your alliance from Discord. The Messages module runs the Chat {% term id="plugin" %}plugin{% /term %}. It copies your alliance chat to a Discord channel, and it sends what people write in that channel back to the game.

Use it when your alliance talks on Discord and you want both chats in one place.

## How it works {% #how-it-works %}

From the game to Discord:

1. Another player writes in your alliance chat.
2. The bot posts the message in your Discord channel, with the player's name in front.

Messages that your own {% term id="game-account" %}game account{% /term %} writes are not copied. That includes the messages the bot sends from Discord, so nothing is posted twice.

From Discord to the game:

1. A person writes in the Discord channel. Messages from other Discord bots are skipped.
2. The bot sends the message to your alliance chat from your game account.
3. By default, the message starts with the writer's Discord nickname, or their display name if they have no nickname. The name shows in the colour of their Discord role.

The bot changes a few things on the way so the game chat can show them:

- A web address becomes a link that players can open in the game.
- Common emoji become game smileys, such as `:)` and `:D`. Other emoji become their name between colons. Emoji without a name are left out.
- Attached files become short TinyURL links, numbered from 0.

## Choose who can post {% #who-can-post %}

{% aside type="caution" id="channel-speaks-for-you" %}
Everything a person posts in the channel shows up in your alliance chat, sent by your game account. Use a channel where only people you trust can write.
{% /aside %}

Turn on **Hide your Discord name** to send Discord messages to the game without the writer's name in front. The message then reads as if your game account wrote it.

## Set up the channel {% #setup %}

1. Pick a text channel in your Discord for the alliance chat. The GGE Command Discord bot must be able to see and post in it.
2. Copy the channel ID. The steps are on [Discord attack alerts](/modules/discord-attacks/#channel-id).
3. Paste the ID into **Channel ID** and save.
4. Start the bot. New alliance chat messages appear in the channel from then on. Older messages are not copied.

